description.narrative:
Protection activities will be implemented in 7 locations (CARE in PIBOR) and aligned with other funding in the 8th location (Akobo County). SSJR partners will reach 294,823 people. The activities include protection prevention measures, child protection, information sharing, capacity strengthening, support to child soldiers/ separated/ unaccompanied children, GBV prevention and response, tracing and reunification. Some of the lessons learnt by the SSJR protection partners that will be incorporated in the design for 2024-2026 are:
 - advocacy strategies should be child-led and community driven; 
- adolescent sexual reproductive health should be integrated into child protection/MHPSS concerns; 
- the engagement of men and boys is integral to the success of GBV outcomes; 
- the importance of awareness in challenging norms and other cultural practices; 
- encouraging more resilient programming to enable community explore more self/community reliant 
approach; 
- complimenting GBV programs with economic empowerment initiatives for women and girls.
The protection partners will adhere to the MHPSS global guidelines, child protection minimum standards, 
child protection area of responsibility case management guidelines and Standard Operating Procedures 
(SOPs), Data Management/protection protocols, IASC Gender with Age Marker, the Washington Group 
Questions, IASC guidelines for disability inclusion in humanitarian action, the Ministry of Health guidelines 
on disability inclusion.
